==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|svá}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*swa}}, {{m|gem-pro|*swē}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*swe}} and {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*se}}. Cognate with Old English {{m|ang|swā}} (English {{m|en|so}}), Old Frisian {{m|ofs|sa}}, Old Saxon {{m|osx|sō}}, Dutch {{m|nl|zo}}, Old High German {{m|goh|sō}} (German {{m|de|so}}), Swedish {{m|sv|så}}, Danish {{m|da|så}}, Gothic {{m|got|𐍃𐍅𐌰}}, Latin {{m|la|si}} (from an earlier form {{m|la|suad}}), Oscan {{m|osc|𐌔𐌅𐌀𐌝|sc=Ital|tr=svaí}}, Umbrian {{m|xum|sve}}, Greek {{m|grc|ὡς}} (earlier '''*ϝος''').

